overweight," or whatever.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:52.290
No, this is like fat
that kind of concentrates

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.780
in your neck and your shoulders.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:58.230
And if you go back to like
pre-climate-controlled times,

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.790
so we're talking like
thousands of years ago,

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:02.690
everybody had way more brown fat,

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:04.560
and they were able to
regulate their temperature

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:07.780
and be cold and not really
have a big deal with it.

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:09.760
But now we've lost all our brown fat

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:13.410
because we've got hoodies and
jackets and climate control.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.587
And so you don't need it.

00:21:14.587 --> 00:21:16.347
And so you quickly lose it,

00:21:16.347 --> 00:21:18.080
but there's all these studies that show.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:19.530
In fact, there was one
study I was looking at.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:23.270
There was these guys
who they slept, I think,

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:28.110
uncovered, out of a blanket,
and it's 68 degrees.

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:30.697
So like 68 degrees without
a blanket, you'd be like,

00:21:30.697 --> 00:21:32.230
"Mm, this is a little uncomfortable,

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:34.750
a little too cold, right,
just a little bit too cold."

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:38.920
And these men did this for like six weeks,

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:41.970
and they all had some
very noticeable increase

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:43.640
in the amount of brown fat.

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.140
And what that ends up doing

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:48.370
is you become way more
tolerant of cold very quickly.

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:50.420
And then the moment they went
back to sleeping regular,

00:21:50.420 --> 00:21:52.740
like within a few weeks
they lost the brown fat.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.690
So you got to keep doing it.

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:57.990
